<h2>John Fox FRAS Biography</h2>
<div class="blocks"><div class="row split reverse wrap"><div class="block media"><p><img alt="" data-nw="427" decoding="async" height="141" loading="lazy" src="/images/science-cafe/john-fox-fras.jpg" width="100"/></p></div><div class="block"><p>John has spent 55 years in the professional photographic arena and has practical experience in all formats of film equipment up to and including 5”x 4” plate cameras. </p><p>He won “Photographer of the Year” in the 1983 Southern Press Radio and Television Awards  and has also won three ILFORD awards during his 32 years as a press photographer, working both in Sussex and Manchester.</p><p>Outside of his press photography adventures John has also photographed over 1,400 weddings during his long career. John switched to digital in 2003 and has embraced  the freedom of shooting and editing digital imagery. Now semi-retired, he has taken the opportunity to pursue  his passion for Astrophotography along with his love of all things video including night sky time lapse imaging. </p><p>John's one day “Astrophotography using a DSLR Camera” courses are a popular event held at the OSC Herstmonceux  and he also teaches the same one day course on behalf of the Royal Photographic Society. </p><p>As a STEM Ambassador and chairperson of Wealden Astronomers Herstmonceux, he gets ample opportunity to pass on his knowledge  and passion for Astrophotography. John, along with other Wealden Astronomers STEM Ambassadors,  attend the Stargazing Evenings at the Observatory Science Centre, Herstmonceux  where they interact with visitors who enjoy looking through the Wealden Astronomers members  amateur telescopes on the lawns, or to pick up vital tips on imaging the night sky using a DSLR camera.</p></div></div></div>
